{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>The righteous</b> — He stated that the enemies of HaShem and His enemies will perish, and the enemies of HaShem are His enemies, in the manner of \"Do I not hate those who hate You, O YHWH\" (Psalm 139:21). He said the opposite of this: the righteous is like a palm tree, which stands for many years. And he said \"the wicked\" in the plural, for they are many, and \"righteous\" in the singular, for they are few. And he likened him to a fruit tree giving choice fruit; also \"he shall flourish and grow\" like a mighty tree in Lebanon, which is the cedar. And he likened the wicked to grass and the flower of the field, which does not stand but a little while."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 92, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:03.581683553Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}